      "coverage": "Convex light-curve reconstruction with approximate thermal size: 108.41 km (catalog ±1.67 km; additional shape and thermal-model uncertainty). Thermal size is used as a volume-scale approximation. An alternative pole remains possible. The grid marks unavailable imagery. The physical size is approximately calibrated by assigning the AKARI thermal effective diameter to the mesh volume-equivalent diameter. Neither source mesh nor spin is modified. Convex inversion supplies only broad outline; no resolved craters, concavities, reflectance or regolith texture can be inferred. Both 2013 convex poles (90,14) and (269,15) remain plausible. Model 557 is a representative solution; neither a smaller model ID nor the ordering in the paper establishes a preferred pole. Use the original unscaled coordinates with an explicitly approximate AKARI thermal-size scale.",
